WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.127
Narrator: What do you think of when

00:00:01.127 --> 00:00:03.630
you hear the word poison?

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.000
Arsenic?

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.540
Cyanide?

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.630
How about water?

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:11.010
Life couldn't exist without water,

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.070
but in the right circumstance,

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:16.233
water can be as dangerous as any poison.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.900
Your kidneys filter out
excess waste and water

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.430
from your bloodstream.

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:27.310
But they can only process
800 to 1,000 milliliters

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:30.250
of water an hour, and
if you somehow managed

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.510
to drink more than that
without throwing up,

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:33.950
you could run into trouble.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.300
Because you're drinking faster

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.580
than your kidneys can process it.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.620
So the excess ends up in your cells.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.770
Normally, your cells are
surrounded by a carefully balanced

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:47.350
solution of sodium and
water, which flows in and out

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:50.120
through tiny holes in
the cellular membrane.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:53.300
So it keeps the sodium
concentration, both in and out

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.130
of the cell, balanced.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:57.160
But when you drink too much water,

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.660
the sodium solution gets diluted.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.840
It's not salty enough.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.780
So some of that excess
water rushes into the cell

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.730
to restore balance.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.340
And that causes it to swell up.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:12.510
Doctors call this water intoxication,

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.610
and it's a big problem.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:18.660
Now, most of your cells can
handle the swelling to a degree,

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:22.960
since soft, flexible tissue
like fat and muscle can stretch.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.920
But for the cells in your
brain, it's another story,

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.560
because your skull isn't stretchy.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:29.840
It's bone.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.960
It's hard, like a rock.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:36.450
So, as your brain swells it
builds up pressure in your head.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.400
At first you might experience
headaches, confusion,

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.740
or drowsiness, but as
the pressure increases,

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:46.460
you risk brain damage,
coma, and even death.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:50.240
And it could all be over
in less than 10 hours.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:54.230
A 64-year-old woman for
example, died the same evening

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:58.960
after drinking between 30
to 40 glasses of water.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:01.270
And a group of US Army trainees suffered

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:04.860
vomiting and seizures after
downing over two liters

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:07.800
per hour after a tough day of training.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:11.513
But it's marathon runners who
need to be especially careful.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.230
A study found that one
in six marathon runners

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:18.010
develop at least mild water intoxication,

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:20.080
because the race stresses their body,

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:21.820
including the kidneys.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:24.760
So they don't excrete
water as efficiently,

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:28.740
which can cause water to back
up into the blood more easily.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:31.600
And the problem isn't unique to water.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.980
For example, the same thing can happen

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:36.610
if you down too much beer at once.

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:38.720
That's called potomania.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:42.620
The good news is, severe
water intoxication is rare,

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:44.790
and is more likely to
happen in people who have

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:47.440
kidney issues, since
they can't process water

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.310
properly to begin with.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:52.660
Plus, there is an easy way to stay safe.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:55.160
The average healthy adult
needs somewhere around

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:57.610
three to four liters of water a day.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.460
And since this can come from food

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:02.430
and other drinks too,
drink when you're thirsty,

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:03.373
and then stop.

